INT. NIGHT FERRY, OBSERVATION DECK - NIGHT

Wind. Salt spray. Empty benches bolted to the deck.

DETECTIVE RUSSELL TEMPLETON-OYELARAN (50s) grips the rail. Beside him, a small woman in a yellow slicker, ANTONIA "TONI" BERGSTROM-ABIODUN (30s), watches the wake.

RUSSELL
You said you'd tell me.

TONI
I did.

RUSSELL
Then tell me.

TONI
Not here.

RUSSELL
Here.

TONI
He's on this boat.

RUSSELL
Who?

TONI
The man in the grey cap.

RUSSELL ^
I didn't see --

TONI
Don't turn around.

Russell turns. A gull cries. The deck is empty. Toni is gone.
